1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,189
Food waste, livestock manure and other
organic waste often contain a lot of water.

2
00:00:07,779 --> 00:00:13,131
The Rapid Fermentation and Drying System
treats this waste inside a sealed vessel,

3
00:00:13,171 --> 00:00:18,457
combining drying and fermentation to turn
it into a dry, easy-to-handle resource.

4
00:00:19,047 --> 00:00:22,831
This video explains how the system
works, the steps of the process,

5
00:00:22,871 --> 00:00:24,942
and how the output can be put to use.

6
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:31,389
Left as it is, wet organic
waste causes several problems.

7
00:00:31,979 --> 00:00:35,848
Odors spread, and insects and
pathogens multiply more easily.

8
00:00:36,438 --> 00:00:40,283
Contaminated liquid can seep out
and pollute soil and waterways.

9
00:00:40,873 --> 00:00:44,864
And when it is piled up or landfilled,
it tends to release methane,

10
00:00:44,904 --> 00:00:46,308
a potent greenhouse gas.

11
00:00:48,867 --> 00:00:53,756
Methane is produced mainly when organic
matter breaks down without enough oxygen.

12
00:00:54,346 --> 00:00:58,012
Inside a waste pile or a
landfill, air cannot reach easily.

13
00:00:58,052 --> 00:01:00,211
These are exactly those conditions.

14
00:01:00,801 --> 00:01:04,703
If the material is mixed and
exposed to air as it breaks down,

15
00:01:04,743 --> 00:01:08,263
what comes out is mainly
carbon dioxide and water vapor.

16
00:01:08,853 --> 00:01:14,760
The Rapid Fermentation and Drying System creates
these aerobic conditions inside a sealed vessel.

17
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:19,435
First, an overview of the whole process.

18
00:01:20,025 --> 00:01:23,427
Organic waste enters the
system through the feed hopper.

19
00:01:23,467 --> 00:01:24,964
Inside the sealed vessel,

20
00:01:25,004 --> 00:01:28,714
it is heated and mixed while
drying and fermentation proceed.

21
00:01:29,304 --> 00:01:36,618
The dried output then passes through a rotating screen that
removes foreign matter and prepares it for use as a resource.

22
00:01:37,208 --> 00:01:41,182
Meanwhile, the moisture from the
waste is drawn off as vapor, cooled,

23
00:01:41,222 --> 00:01:42,520
and recovered as water.

24
00:01:45,067 --> 00:01:47,219
Two actions sit at the
heart of the system.

25
00:01:47,809 --> 00:01:49,532
The first is removing water.

26
00:01:49,572 --> 00:01:55,388
Lowering the pressure inside the vessel lets
water evaporate at a relatively low temperature.

27
00:01:55,978 --> 00:01:58,934
The second is activating
indigenous microbes,

28
00:01:58,974 --> 00:02:02,129
the microorganisms already
present in the waste.

29
00:02:02,169 --> 00:02:05,857
They break down organic matter
as fermentation proceeds.

30
00:02:06,447 --> 00:02:10,803
Combining the two turns wet feedstock
into a dry product in a short time.

31
00:02:13,367 --> 00:02:16,100
Let's take a closer look at
how reduced pressure helps.

32
00:02:16,690 --> 00:02:20,591
The temperature at which water boils
depends on the surrounding pressure.

33
00:02:20,631 --> 00:02:23,399
The lower the pressure, the
lower the boiling point.

34
00:02:23,989 --> 00:02:29,295
It is the same reason water boils below
100 degrees Celsius on a high mountain.

35
00:02:29,885 --> 00:02:32,039
By reducing the pressure in the vessel,

36
00:02:32,079 --> 00:02:36,146
the system removes moisture efficiently
without overheating the material.

37
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:42,189
The main unit is a sealed,
horizontal processing vessel.

38
00:02:42,779 --> 00:02:47,487
In one typical configuration, heat
reaches the material through three paths:

39
00:02:47,527 --> 00:02:50,735
a jacket around the vessel,
a hollow rotating shaft,

40
00:02:50,775 --> 00:02:52,859
and the mixing paddles themselves.

41
00:02:53,449 --> 00:02:56,954
Spiral paddles keep the material
circulating through the vessel,

42
00:02:56,994 --> 00:02:59,003
evening out temperature and moisture.

43
00:02:59,593 --> 00:03:05,127
The vapor that is released is drawn out from the
top of the vessel and sent on to the recovery stage.

44
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:10,764
Operation is divided
into three main stages.

45
00:03:11,354 --> 00:03:12,393
In the first stage,

46
00:03:12,433 --> 00:03:16,254
the vessel is depressurized to
reduce the moisture in the feedstock.

47
00:03:16,844 --> 00:03:17,982
In the second stage,

48
00:03:18,022 --> 00:03:23,754
outside air is brought in so that microbes can
break down the organic matter through fermentation.

49
00:03:24,344 --> 00:03:27,850
Finally, the pressure is lowered
again for a finishing dry,

50
00:03:27,890 --> 00:03:30,735
and the material is
discharged as a dry product.

51
00:03:31,325 --> 00:03:35,036
The time and temperature of each
stage are set for each project,

52
00:03:35,076 --> 00:03:37,497
based on the type and amount of feedstock.

53
00:03:40,067 --> 00:03:42,559
So what happens to the water
taken out of the waste?

54
00:03:43,149 --> 00:03:47,958
Vapor drawn from the vessel is cooled in
a condenser and turns back into water.

55
00:03:48,548 --> 00:03:52,275
A gas-liquid separator then splits
the flow into water and air,

56
00:03:52,315 --> 00:03:55,026
and the water is collected
as recovered water.

57
00:03:55,616 --> 00:03:59,974
How far the recovered water and heat
can be reused is studied for each site,

58
00:04:00,014 --> 00:04:01,479
based on local conditions.

59
00:04:04,033 --> 00:04:06,497
Odor control is built into the same flow.

60
00:04:07,087 --> 00:04:11,716
The vessel stays sealed during treatment,
so odorous air does not easily escape.

61
00:04:12,306 --> 00:04:16,205
Vapor passes through condensation
and gas-liquid separation,

62
00:04:16,245 --> 00:04:21,852
and the remaining air is deodorized by
filtration before it is drawn out and released.

63
00:04:22,442 --> 00:04:24,462
Compared with piling waste outdoors,

64
00:04:24,502 --> 00:04:27,208
this design makes it
harder for odors to spread.

65
00:04:29,767 --> 00:04:34,128
Because treatment takes place in a sealed
vessel, it is clear where everything goes.

66
00:04:34,718 --> 00:04:36,135
There are three outlets:

67
00:04:36,175 --> 00:04:39,169
the dried product, water
recovered from the vapor,

68
00:04:39,209 --> 00:04:42,204
and exhaust air that is
deodorized before release.

69
00:04:42,794 --> 00:04:46,548
The share of each depends on the
moisture content and type of feedstock.

70
00:04:47,138 --> 00:04:51,725
With only a few outlets, quantities and
quality are easy to measure and record,

71
00:04:51,765 --> 00:04:53,072
which helps management.

72
00:04:55,633 --> 00:04:58,992
Five indicators are monitored
to keep operation stable.

73
00:04:59,582 --> 00:05:03,437
Temperature, pressure, moisture, odor,
and the condition of the product.

74
00:05:04,027 --> 00:05:07,345
Samples of the product are
taken, analyzed and recorded,

75
00:05:07,385 --> 00:05:11,963
and the results are used to judge whether
the quality suits its intended use.

76
00:05:14,533 --> 00:05:18,401
Candidate feedstocks cover a
wide range of organic waste:

77
00:05:18,441 --> 00:05:22,652
food waste and food residues,
livestock manure, crop residues,

78
00:05:22,692 --> 00:05:24,915
and vegetable waste from markets.

79
00:05:25,505 --> 00:05:30,487
Possible uses for the product include
organic fertilizer and soil conditioner,

80
00:05:30,527 --> 00:05:34,285
as well as animal bedding,
animal feed, and fuel feedstock.

81
00:05:34,875 --> 00:05:38,630
Which feedstocks can be accepted,
and where the product can be used,

82
00:05:38,670 --> 00:05:42,090
is confirmed through quality
testing and local laws and rules.

83
00:05:44,633 --> 00:05:49,826
Returning the product to local farmland as
organic fertilizer creates a resource loop.

84
00:05:50,416 --> 00:05:51,922
Organic waste from homes,

85
00:05:51,962 --> 00:05:57,180
markets and farms becomes a resource in the
system and is used to build healthy soil,

86
00:05:57,220 --> 00:06:00,396
and the crops grown there
return to people's tables.

87
00:06:00,986 --> 00:06:06,204
What used to be disposed of as waste becomes a
resource that circulates within the community.

88
00:06:08,767 --> 00:06:13,947
Greenhouse gas reductions are evaluated
by first deciding exactly what to count.

89
00:06:14,537 --> 00:06:17,576
The boundary runs from where
the waste is generated,

90
00:06:17,616 --> 00:06:21,839
through transport and treatment in
the system, to its use as a resource.

91
00:06:22,429 --> 00:06:28,051
Emissions from transport fuel and from the
electricity and heat used in treatment are added up,

92
00:06:28,091 --> 00:06:33,832
and compared with the methane that landfilling or
similar disposal would otherwise have released.

93
00:06:34,422 --> 00:06:38,713
The actual reduction is calculated
for each project within this boundary.

94
00:06:41,267 --> 00:06:43,393
This system creates two kinds of value.

95
00:06:43,983 --> 00:06:46,051
The first is taking on waste treatment,

96
00:06:46,091 --> 00:06:49,025
which eases the burden on
those who generate the waste.

97
00:06:49,615 --> 00:06:54,104
The second is delivering the product as
a resource, such as organic fertilizer.

98
00:06:54,694 --> 00:06:57,256
With treatment and
resources as two pillars,

99
00:06:57,296 --> 00:07:00,509
the aim is a model that can
be sustained as a business.

100
00:07:03,067 --> 00:07:06,304
Many stakeholders are involved
in putting the system to work.

101
00:07:06,894 --> 00:07:11,655
Households, markets, food factories and
livestock farms that generate waste;

102
00:07:11,695 --> 00:07:14,561
the local government
that supports the scheme;

103
00:07:14,601 --> 00:07:16,709
the operator that runs the system;

104
00:07:16,749 --> 00:07:20,121
and the farmers and local
users who use the resources.

105
00:07:20,711 --> 00:07:22,118
With each playing its part,

106
00:07:22,158 --> 00:07:26,084
waste treatment and resource use are
linked together within the community.

107
00:07:28,733 --> 00:07:35,464
The Rapid Fermentation and Drying System turns organic
waste into resources that communities can put to use.

108
00:07:36,054 --> 00:07:37,257
Thank you for watching.
